1
00:00:00,024 --> 00:00:04,390
ROIS prices every crew-recovery decision. A cost set groups the cost items to charge against; each item’s Calculation Workbench shows the money math.

2
00:00:04,390 --> 00:00:08,758
A cost set is the bundle of priced items a recovery run is scored against.

3
00:00:08,758 --> 00:00:10,060
Open Cost Sets under Legality.

4
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:11,010
“Daily Recovery” is the default cost set — the starter library ROIS scores against.

5
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:14,566
It bundles the individual cost items the optimizer charges for each decision.

6
00:00:14,566 --> 00:00:18,932
Cost templates are the reusable cost items — let’s open the first two.

7
00:00:18,932 --> 00:00:19,982
Switch to Cost Templates.

8
00:00:19,982 --> 00:00:21,194
1002 — Pay above guaranteed hours: crew are guaranteed a monthly floor; only credit above it costs money.

9
00:00:21,194 --> 00:00:22,134
The Calculation Workbench runs the default case live: 84h + 6.75h added → $712.50 above the guarantee floor.

10
00:00:22,134 --> 00:00:26,019
Only credit above the floor becomes incremental cash, priced through the overtime tiers.

11
00:00:26,019 --> 00:00:27,326
1003 — Airport standby credit: standby time first converts into credit.

12
00:00:27,326 --> 00:00:28,261
That standby credit is added to pairing credit, then any hours over guarantee are priced through the linked GH policy.

13
00:00:28,261 --> 00:00:32,468
Same workbench, a different calculator — each cost item explains exactly how it turns an action into cash.

14
00:00:32,468 --> 00:00:36,843
Cost sets group the items; each item’s workbench shows how ROIS prices a recovery decision.
